# rule.always.enskill-the-tactics-you-discover

**when you repeat a sequence of operations, that sequence is a tactic, and it is owed a skill.**

this is the DISCOVER half. `rule.always.entool-the-skills-you-touch` is the UPGRADE half. one loop:

```
discover a repeated sequence → ENSKILL it → notice the leftover brain work → ENTOOL it
```

⇒ **enskill creates the artifact. entool raises its rung.** an unenskilled tactic has no rung to raise; an enskilled tactic left at 💧 fluid forever still costs a brain every use.

the ladder: 0 🧠 tribal → 1 📚 brief → 2 💪💧 fluid skill → 3 💪🔩 rigid skill → 4 💪🪨 solid skill. **all five are tools.** enskill is the step off rung 0.

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| you ran the **same sequence a second time** | 🔴 the strongest cue. enskill it now — the repeat already proved it |
| you **scroll back to copy a command** you ran earlier | your scrollback does a skill's job |
| you chain 3+ commands where each feeds the next | the chain is one tactic, not three steps |
| you **explain a procedure** to someone (or a future self) | you just spoke the skill aloud — write it |
| you think *"the trick is to run X before Y"* | that order constraint is exactly the knowledge worth capture |
| you keep a **private note** of steps | a private note is an unshared skill |
| a sequence is **easy to run and hard to recall** | the highest-value case |
| the steps need **judgment at several points**, in an order that matters | 🗿 **pave a route**, not a linear skill |
| you went **offroad** and reached the end | the path you found IS the artifact. leave a route behind |

## .the test

> **"could the next traveler run this without me in the room?"**

- yes, from what is written → enskilled
- yes, **but they would ask me one question** → **that question is the whole point.** it marks the undiscoverable step
- no, judgment at **one** point → leave it with the brain, and say so
- no, judgment at **several** points, in an order that matters → 🗿 **a route**

then: **"how much could run with no brain at all?"** — write it at that rung today, not the fluid version out of haste.

## 🗿 .when brains are required along the way — pave a route

a route is stones + guards. the brain still does the work at every stone; the route retires the **order** (what precedes what), the **omission** (the guard refuses first), and the **rediscovery**.

⇒ **a skill paves a sequence of commands. a route paves a sequence of judgments.**

🟡 **a route IS a 🔩 rigid skill — rung 3**, not a category beside the ladder: a deterministic transport with probabilistic cargo. and **do not route what could be entooled** — a route around deterministic work charges imagine cost at every stone.

**offroad is legitimate — and it owes a route.** the exploration happened anyway; to end it with pavement turns a one-time cost into a permanent asset.

## .what a skill owes

idempotent · named for the **motive**, not the mechanism · fails loud and names the fix · discoverable via `--help` · **owned by the right tree** — a tactic whose home is another repo is re-seeded there.

## .anti-patterns

the third repeat by hand · the scrollback tactic · the private note · **the premature skill** (run once, enskilled from a guess — wait for the second run) · **the offroad trip with no pavement left behind**.

blocker: a procedure explained with no durable artifact · an offroad exploration that reached its end and left no route. nitpick: written at 💧 where 🔩 was in reach · a route laid over deterministic work.
